[[Summer Break Cats (Gauntlet)|Summer Break Cats]]<br>
[[Infernal Tower]]<br>
[[Citadel#Traitless|Traitless Citadel]]
|money drop = 1,600¢ - 6,320¢
}}

==Enemy==
Has very slow attack speed, and negligible damage, but can stall your team for a long time with its long range, lots of HP and freeze ability, meaning they can be annoying as support. Their freeze is not too bad, as it lasts for only a single second. Due to their lack of speed, they are used to protect the base from damage.

==Strategy==
You really have nothing to fear. This enemy will easily fall to almost any cat with [[:Category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|freeze immunty]] due to its very low damage. On top of that, it has no immunities, meaning you can either knock it behind the base or freeze it using [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-traitless]] cats. It can even be ignored entirely by hitting the base using certain cats with [[:Category:Omni Strike Cats|piercing range]]. If killing it is necessary, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] can get the job done fast.

